  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to the transportation of liquefied natural and petroleum gas, and to repeal certain provisions of such law relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S2823",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2823-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §23-1713 subs 1, 3, & 4, amd §§23-1713, 23-1715 & 23-1717, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2823\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the environmental conservation law,\nin relation to the transportation of liquefied natural and petroleum\ngas, and to repeal certain provisions of such law relating thereto\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo amend the environmental conservation law to repeal paragraphs b and\nc of subdivision 2 and paragraph c of subdivision 3 of section 23-1709\nof the environmental conservation law.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 - Repeals paragraphs b and c of subdivision 2 and paragraph\nc of subdivision 3 of section 23-1709 of the environmental\nconservation law and instead requires those that transport liquefied\nnatural gas and petroleum gas to comply with all applicable federal\nand state laws and regulations and have a valid hazardous waste\nmaterials safety permit as issued by the Federal motor carrier safety\nadministration.\n\nSection 2 - Sets forth the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nLiquefied natural gas (LNG) is a domestic alternative fuel for heavy\nduty trucking. LNG is becoming popular because it is cheaper and\ncleaner than diesel - and it is a domestic energy source. In 2015 the\nDepartment of Environmental Conservation promulgated regulations for\nthe siting, building and operating of liquefied natural gas facilities\nand petroleum gas facilities, however, the department lacked the\nstatutory authority to allow for the intrastate transportation of\nthese fuels on New York's roads. This legislation would allow for such\ntransportation and increase the environmental and economic benefits\noffered by this less expensive, cleaner burning fuel.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016- S.4242\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
